Test Case: Legacy BDH vs NCMI – Declined Application Volume

Business Requirement: Validate that declined application volumes are aligned between Legacy BDH and NCMI BDP using equivalent business definitions.

Test Performed: Compared Legacy BDH Decline volume against the sum of six NCMI application decline measures for September Decision Month. Reviewed underlying SQL calculation logic.

Expected Result: Declined application volumes should be broadly aligned where equivalent business definitions are applied.

Actual Result: Legacy BDH Decline: 22,462; NCMI decline components: 24,707. Difference: +2,245 (+10.00%). Investigation identified that some BDP decline measures include final application statuses other than DECLINE. Metric definitions require further clarification before confirming alignment.

Status: PENDING CLARIFICATION

Evidence: Legacy BDH Decline pivot result, Snowflake decline reconciliation results and NCMI SQL logic.



SELECT
    SUM(
        COALESCE(API_ACCEPT_ON_US_ACCEPT_APPLICATION_DECLINE_COUNT, 0)
      + COALESCE(API_ACCEPT_ON_US_REFER_APPLICATION_DECLINE_COUNT, 0)
      + COALESCE(API_ACCEPT_ON_US_DECLINE_APPLICATION_DECLINE_COUNT, 0)
      + COALESCE(DIRECT_ON_US_ACCEPT_APPLICATION_DECLINE_COUNT, 0)
      + COALESCE(DIRECT_ON_US_REFER_APPLICATION_DECLINE_COUNT, 0)
      + COALESCE(DIRECT_ON_US_DECLINE_APPLICATION_DECLINE_COUNT, 0)
    ) AS APPLICATION_DECLINE_COUNT
FROM BDP_UK_CARDS.FACT_CARD_AGGREGATOR_APPLICATION_SUMMARY
WHERE APPLICATION_DECISION_DATE >= DATE '2026-09-01'
  AND APPLICATION_DECISION_DATE < DATE '2026-10-01';



